--- rate, measured over 10 s on the consumer
err=4096 results seen by B: 44810 -> 59388  => 1457 per second
(retry="5 +" is configured and is never consulted on this path)

--- does it heal?  sampling every 30 s
  t+ 70s  cumulative err=4096 on B: 102761
  t+100s  cumulative err=4096 on B: 146069
  t+130s  cumulative err=4096 on B: 189324

=== 5. the cure: have the missing serverID write one entry
serverID 002 is node B.  One write at B re-enters SID 002 in
A's log DB contextCSN via syncprov_new_ctxcsn().  minCSN is not touched.
adding new entry "cn=cure,dc=example,dc=org"


--- A's log DB after the cure write
dn: cn=accesslog
minCSN: 20261003200751.068026Z#000000#001#000000
minCSN: 20261003200751.075975Z#000000#002#000000
contextCSN: 20261003200751.068026Z#000000#001#000000
contextCSN: 20261003201008.887803Z#000000#002#000000


--- rate after the cure
err=4096 on B: 189570 -> 189570  => 0 per second
(was 1457 per second before; cumulative before cure: 189561)

